            <ArticleTitle>Persistent high-altitude headache and aguesia without anosmia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>340-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>High-altitude headache and taste dysfunction are usually cured within a few months by descent to sea level. We studied a patient who had persistent bitemporal throbbing headache with the associated findings of high-altitude headache syndrome 15 years after a compression chamber accident. He also had loss of taste without loss of smell since the incident.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
